      <room>H.1302</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Taxonomy: Drupals powerful classification system</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Drupal</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Taxonomy is Drupal&amp;#39;s classification system. In this talk Bart explains how it differs from a regular categorisation system and what Drupal core and contributed modules offer to manipulate, browse and apply it.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk gives a short explanation about what Taxonomy is and what it does in simple and clear terminology. Bart briefly describes the history of Taxonomy from Drupal 4 to Drupal 7. Finally he discusses when to use Book.module and when Taxonomy for arranging your content.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="741">Bart Feenstra</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>